[{:db/id 17592186100943 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3b37913a-69c1-5101-b52b-7d6c5fd60a19" "question-52ad75c1-24f1-5969-9d6c-0ceaa8d872d2" "question-337615da-7bae-5da8-aef5-ed48be968edc" "question-47725b1d-6489-53a4-9d3a-6bd1c0f75d94"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100779 :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?\n\nI. $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} t} = 56y-7y^2$\n\nII. $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} t} = 56-7y^2$\n\nIII. $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} t} = 56y^2-7$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100942 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cfc9e704-11ab-5799-a5b1-c0cc751bf228" "question-e56756c2-a487-52f8-beba-b87d8eaed329" "question-6009a1c0-18f1-5130-b32c-9c18394dafe6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b37913a-69c1-5101-b52b-7d6c5fd60a19" :question/id #uuid "3b37913a-69c1-5101-b52b-7d6c5fd60a19" :question/math-academy-id "q-83851" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=55y-11{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=11y(5-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=11,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-763f4e8a-a7fa-5aa1-8400-9b9749f4b5ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-763f4e8a-a7fa-5aa1-8400-9b9749f4b5ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "763f4e8a-a7fa-5aa1-8400-9b9749f4b5ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5e2458c3-7905-560b-b228-5e789283c915" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bde69846-e1b3-5fef-932a-67166e89832f" "answer-1d5f4efc-0abf-57f1-ba32-0185947e100a" "answer-c477b860-dcba-5e72-8b0f-808774233cb4" "answer-5e2458c3-7905-560b-b228-5e789283c915" "answer-19c12834-371c-5f63-bdfb-02c2541583fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde69846-e1b3-5fef-932a-67166e89832f" :answer/id #uuid "bde69846-e1b3-5fef-932a-67166e89832f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=45y+5{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d5f4efc-0abf-57f1-ba32-0185947e100a" :answer/id #uuid "1d5f4efc-0abf-57f1-ba32-0185947e100a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=5+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c477b860-dcba-5e72-8b0f-808774233cb4" :answer/id #uuid "c477b860-dcba-5e72-8b0f-808774233cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=550-11y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e2458c3-7905-560b-b228-5e789283c915" :answer/id #uuid "5e2458c3-7905-560b-b228-5e789283c915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=55y-11{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19c12834-371c-5f63-bdfb-02c2541583fe" :answer/id #uuid "19c12834-371c-5f63-bdfb-02c2541583fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=5{y}^{2}-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-52ad75c1-24f1-5969-9d6c-0ceaa8d872d2" :question/id #uuid "52ad75c1-24f1-5969-9d6c-0ceaa8d872d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-83850" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=2y(10-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17f1684b-41e0-59c7-9d1d-0134c261dee4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17f1684b-41e0-59c7-9d1d-0134c261dee4" :answer-field/id #uuid "17f1684b-41e0-59c7-9d1d-0134c261dee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c745c03-98a8-571c-aa79-f32d40ebf4e1" "answer-26312008-2455-55a8-bc1d-9b869b44fda8" "answer-cf11bce7-e4f3-5e71-8383-6e355495bc3c" "answer-1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" "answer-d3fc1100-2d33-56a2-a856-01e2f5f30f90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c745c03-98a8-571c-aa79-f32d40ebf4e1" :answer/id #uuid "2c745c03-98a8-571c-aa79-f32d40ebf4e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26312008-2455-55a8-bc1d-9b869b44fda8" :answer/id #uuid "26312008-2455-55a8-bc1d-9b869b44fda8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20-2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf11bce7-e4f3-5e71-8383-6e355495bc3c" :answer/id #uuid "cf11bce7-e4f3-5e71-8383-6e355495bc3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y+2{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" :answer/id #uuid "1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y-2{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3fc1100-2d33-56a2-a856-01e2f5f30f90" :answer/id #uuid "d3fc1100-2d33-56a2-a856-01e2f5f30f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20{y}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-337615da-7bae-5da8-aef5-ed48be968edc" :question/id #uuid "337615da-7bae-5da8-aef5-ed48be968edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-83852" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=y-3{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y(\\frac{1}{3}-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=3,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6064b7d-2ce9-5405-a285-35f32d2b4760"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6064b7d-2ce9-5405-a285-35f32d2b4760" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6064b7d-2ce9-5405-a285-35f32d2b4760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-899816c6-722e-5949-9ce4-1a89698b454a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a58cff2-1268-5a47-8339-f8986d6b3b53" "answer-9d888226-313c-58ec-b603-27ecf200a67a" "answer-fff1f2be-796e-56e8-9751-6260916e4506" "answer-e86aa13e-6c97-5b82-b6ff-679f462956c1" "answer-899816c6-722e-5949-9ce4-1a89698b454a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a58cff2-1268-5a47-8339-f8986d6b3b53" :answer/id #uuid "5a58cff2-1268-5a47-8339-f8986d6b3b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d888226-313c-58ec-b603-27ecf200a67a" :answer/id #uuid "9d888226-313c-58ec-b603-27ecf200a67a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=4+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fff1f2be-796e-56e8-9751-6260916e4506" :answer/id #uuid "fff1f2be-796e-56e8-9751-6260916e4506" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=9-{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e86aa13e-6c97-5b82-b6ff-679f462956c1" :answer/id #uuid "e86aa13e-6c97-5b82-b6ff-679f462956c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y+3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-899816c6-722e-5949-9ce4-1a89698b454a" :answer/id #uuid "899816c6-722e-5949-9ce4-1a89698b454a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y-3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-47725b1d-6489-53a4-9d3a-6bd1c0f75d94" :question/id #uuid "47725b1d-6489-53a4-9d3a-6bd1c0f75d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-119267" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=35y-7{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=7y(5-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=7,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05ec70e4-e3ba-524d-be45-20e5c451f94b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05ec70e4-e3ba-524d-be45-20e5c451f94b" :answer-field/id #uuid "05ec70e4-e3ba-524d-be45-20e5c451f94b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-076adf41-55fa-5e02-a5f4-92e1a61c4181" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ccb0db6-5ea4-55e4-8c9d-e19190d4f9ec" "answer-c5230433-2add-5000-ad4e-95ef2322db26" "answer-3ebf0f82-e343-52b7-8a49-05d015118207" "answer-c6b4484f-b8cf-59f6-8eb0-156f59685802" "answer-076adf41-55fa-5e02-a5f4-92e1a61c4181"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ccb0db6-5ea4-55e4-8c9d-e19190d4f9ec" :answer/id #uuid "4ccb0db6-5ea4-55e4-8c9d-e19190d4f9ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=35-7{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5230433-2add-5000-ad4e-95ef2322db26" :answer/id #uuid "c5230433-2add-5000-ad4e-95ef2322db26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=35y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ebf0f82-e343-52b7-8a49-05d015118207" :answer/id #uuid "3ebf0f82-e343-52b7-8a49-05d015118207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=35y+7{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6b4484f-b8cf-59f6-8eb0-156f59685802" :answer/id #uuid "c6b4484f-b8cf-59f6-8eb0-156f59685802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=35y-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-076adf41-55fa-5e02-a5f4-92e1a61c4181" :answer/id #uuid "076adf41-55fa-5e02-a5f4-92e1a61c4181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=35y-7{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfc9e704-11ab-5799-a5b1-c0cc751bf228" :question/id #uuid "cfc9e704-11ab-5799-a5b1-c0cc751bf228" :question/math-academy-id "q-83855" :question/problem "A rumor is spreading in a school of $2\\,000$ students. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ who have heard the rumor is jointly proportional to the number of people who have heard the rumor at time $t,$ measured in hours, and the number who have not heard the rumor. If the constant of proportionality is $2.5,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the rumor's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the number of people who have heard the rumor at time $t,$ and the number who have not, the number of people who have heard the rumor follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=2.5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=2\\,000.$ Therefore, the number of people who heard the rumor is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2.5P(2\\,000-P).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-611d3f14-6e92-5707-9d1c-74f01cafe308"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-611d3f14-6e92-5707-9d1c-74f01cafe308" :answer-field/id #uuid "611d3f14-6e92-5707-9d1c-74f01cafe308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-df46b27d-b130-5ffa-8f32-a6057c1940a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2fabba3-d0eb-5536-9a95-97abc2710798" "answer-b5f243f9-3128-53cf-8e9c-a561972a655a" "answer-df46b27d-b130-5ffa-8f32-a6057c1940a8" "answer-a406afc4-d960-5034-b51e-8c31d270b58b" "answer-b5266803-3e57-51fe-9003-3e15528da116"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2fabba3-d0eb-5536-9a95-97abc2710798" :answer/id #uuid "a2fabba3-d0eb-5536-9a95-97abc2710798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-2.5P(2\\,000-P)." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5f243f9-3128-53cf-8e9c-a561972a655a" :answer/id #uuid "b5f243f9-3128-53cf-8e9c-a561972a655a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2.5P(2\\,000+P)." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df46b27d-b130-5ffa-8f32-a6057c1940a8" :answer/id #uuid "df46b27d-b130-5ffa-8f32-a6057c1940a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2.5P(2\\,000-P)." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a406afc4-d960-5034-b51e-8c31d270b58b" :answer/id #uuid "a406afc4-d960-5034-b51e-8c31d270b58b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,000P(2.5+P)." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5266803-3e57-51fe-9003-3e15528da116" :answer/id #uuid "b5266803-3e57-51fe-9003-3e15528da116" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=2\\,000P(2.5-P)." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e56756c2-a487-52f8-beba-b87d8eaed329" :question/id #uuid "e56756c2-a487-52f8-beba-b87d8eaed329" :question/math-academy-id "q-83862" :question/problem "The growth rate of the woodpecker population $P(t)$ in a certain forest is jointly proportional to the woodpecker population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the woodpecker population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,1$ and the maximum possible woodpecker population is $10\\,000,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the woodpecker population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the woodpecker population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the woodpecker population, the woodpecker population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,1,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=10\\,000.$ Therefore, the woodpecker population is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,1P(10\\,000-P).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b8afcb64-7f3e-534f-a7ec-9869fa2663b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b8afcb64-7f3e-534f-a7ec-9869fa2663b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8afcb64-7f3e-534f-a7ec-9869fa2663b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76b57d70-a086-5a76-ad08-1757bf1a92fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36f03a9c-6c86-514e-8536-0c6bba5a3abf" "answer-25935ef1-27a2-5178-a4d2-d936bbae9e34" "answer-76b57d70-a086-5a76-ad08-1757bf1a92fd" "answer-94d0e760-c927-55f9-8532-b3496e6146ba" "answer-a1bd8bc3-8421-52dd-bc14-38e7879c5978"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36f03a9c-6c86-514e-8536-0c6bba5a3abf" :answer/id #uuid "36f03a9c-6c86-514e-8536-0c6bba5a3abf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-0.000\\,1P(10\\,000-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25935ef1-27a2-5178-a4d2-d936bbae9e34" :answer/id #uuid "25935ef1-27a2-5178-a4d2-d936bbae9e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,1P(10\\,000+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76b57d70-a086-5a76-ad08-1757bf1a92fd" :answer/id #uuid "76b57d70-a086-5a76-ad08-1757bf1a92fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,1P(10\\,000-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94d0e760-c927-55f9-8532-b3496e6146ba" :answer/id #uuid "94d0e760-c927-55f9-8532-b3496e6146ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=10\\,000P(0.000\\,1+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1bd8bc3-8421-52dd-bc14-38e7879c5978" :answer/id #uuid "a1bd8bc3-8421-52dd-bc14-38e7879c5978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=10\\,000P(0.000\\,1-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6009a1c0-18f1-5130-b32c-9c18394dafe6" :question/id #uuid "6009a1c0-18f1-5130-b32c-9c18394dafe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-85975" :question/problem "Some viral content on the internet starts spreading through an audience of $60\\,000$ people. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ who have seen the content is jointly proportional to the number of people who have seen the content at time $t,$ measured in hours, and the number who have not. If the constant of proportionality is $0.75,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the growth rate of people who have seen the content is *jointly* proportional to the number of people who have seen the content at time $t,$ and the number who have not, the number of people who have seen the content follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.75,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=60\\,000.$ Therefore, the number of people who have seen the content is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.75P(60\\,000-P).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a96f53c-28f1-5a63-8cc1-08c4c076a8a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a96f53c-28f1-5a63-8cc1-08c4c076a8a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a96f53c-28f1-5a63-8cc1-08c4c076a8a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d881d9cc-7679-5e20-949e-5c6732e6c221" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74b013fb-7bc8-5cdf-9d89-9d9560979c6d" "answer-2734d77f-afd6-5eac-babe-fd41a107ee1c" "answer-d881d9cc-7679-5e20-949e-5c6732e6c221" "answer-14a10537-d01c-588a-af50-1725a012a2bf" "answer-f9f11950-bdd9-5f8f-89ec-bd8c9b4bc5af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74b013fb-7bc8-5cdf-9d89-9d9560979c6d" :answer/id #uuid "74b013fb-7bc8-5cdf-9d89-9d9560979c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-0.75P(60\\,000-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2734d77f-afd6-5eac-babe-fd41a107ee1c" :answer/id #uuid "2734d77f-afd6-5eac-babe-fd41a107ee1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.75P(60\\,000+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d881d9cc-7679-5e20-949e-5c6732e6c221" :answer/id #uuid "d881d9cc-7679-5e20-949e-5c6732e6c221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.75P(60\\,000-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14a10537-d01c-588a-af50-1725a012a2bf" :answer/id #uuid "14a10537-d01c-588a-af50-1725a012a2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=60\\,000P(0.75+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9f11